{
 "indicator": {
  "definition": {
   "definition": "The Liquidity Adjustment Facility covers the Reserve Bank's operations that inject liquidity into, or absorb liquidity from, the banking system: overnight and term repo/reverse repo (fixed and variable rate), the Standing Deposit Facility and the Marginal Standing Facility. Net injection (+)/absorption (-) is the net liquidity position — Repo + MSF + SLF less Reverse Repo less SDF — published daily in the 'Money Market Operations' release and weekly in the WSS 'Liquidity Operations by RBI' table. The SDF, at which RBI accepts uncollateralised overnight deposits from LAF participants, is the floor of the corridor (25 basis points below the repo rate) and replaced the fixed reverse repo as the floor in April 2022; the MSF, at which banks may borrow overnight by dipping into their SLR portfolio up to a limit, is the ceiling (25 basis points above the repo rate).",
   "source_name": "Reserve Bank of India — 'Money Market Operations' release; WSS 'Liquidity Operations by RBI' (item 8)",
   "source_url": "https://rbi.org.in/Scripts/BS_PressReleaseDisplay.aspx?prid=62917",
   "term": "Liquidity Adjustment Facility: net injection (+) / absorption (-), SDF and MSF"
  },
